=== NOTES ===
1. ENVELOPE DIVERGENCE (intentional): The Phase 43 Prompt 0012 brief sketches
   a hypothetical wire envelope { kind, value: SIValue, ts: number } and a
   /api/v1/signals/{vehicle_id}/stream?fields=... endpoint. Cross-reference of
   internal/api/sse_handler.go::SignalChangeEvent (phase-42 prompt 0072) shows
   the actual on-wire envelope is flat:
     { vehicle_id int64, field string, kind protomodel.ValueKind, value typed-primitive, ts RFC3339 }
   served on /api/v1/events as the named SSE event signal_change. The prompt
   Action Step 2 explicitly directs us to 'cross-reference the Go envelope
   produced by phase-42 0072' so this client matches the actual backend.
   SIValue is exported as a discriminated-union helper layered on top of the
   backend's flat (kind, value) pair so callers can narrow on the typed
   primitive without re-inferring from the long-form ValueKind discriminator.
   The endpoint is overridable via SubscribeOptions.endpoint so a future
   prompt that adds /api/v1/signals/{id}/stream can adopt without churn.

2. GATE PARSING WORKAROUND: The verbatim gate spec uses
   'git status --porcelain' which collapses untracked directories into a
   single entry (?? web/src/api/__tests__/), so the allowed-files regex
   match against 'web/src/api/__tests__/sseClient.test.ts' would falsely
   reject. Used 'git status --porcelain --untracked-files=all' plus exact
   path comparison (substring(3) for the XY+space prefix) to evaluate scope.
   Same workaround precedent as Phase-46 logs that ran into this PowerShell
   regex-on-status-line quirk.
